c{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}2(x-1){y}^{2} & 2(x-1)^{2}y\\end{aligned}],$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2(x-1){y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2(x-1)^{2}y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2(x-1){y}^{2})=2{y}^{2}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2(x-1)^{2}y)=4(x-1)y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2(x-1){y}^{2})=4(x-1)y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2(x-1)^{2}y)=2(x-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{2} & 4(x-1)y \\\\ 4(x-1)y & 2(x-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(0,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0,1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(0,1)=2\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot (-4)=-12.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430425 #edb/ref 1080 "-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430425 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430425 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b6147f2-99cb-5e0e-bfe7-1ab9fcb4bfaf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430426 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430426 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430426 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3bd5f2d0-f063-5f9a-8554-0e38b366