b/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430448 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:{{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} & 2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}],$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x})=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x})=\\frac{2y}{x}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{2y}{x} & 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=(-1)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 2=-4.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186481463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1045 "The Second Derivative of a Multivariable Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186481451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480731 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "0d220057-0079-57e6-bb5c-eb3461a91e72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480829 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480829 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480829 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2fca28ad-f59e-5a0a-bb4c-0662386d1e94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480831 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480831 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186480831 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3075a971-db98-5b66-a3d1-9af12fdf7be7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481006 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481006 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481006 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8cb3995c-cc